BUF.excerpt:
) Periods of rain and gusty winds through this evening.
) Much colder tonight through Saturday night with a few wet snowflakes possible early Saturday morning.
) An extended period of dry and warmer weather begins Sunday and lasts most of next week.

CTP.excerpt:
) A potent cold front preceded and accompanied by an anomalously strong low-level WSW jet of 45-55 kts will move SE across PA today with a severe threat focused this aftn/evening.
) Windy with the first snowflakes of the season possible on the higher terrain of the north tonight/Sat morning
) Cold weather may end the growing season for many places this weekend, with Sun morning the coldest.

RLX.excerpt:
) High confidence in a strong cold front that will bring showers, storms, and gusty winds today.
) High confidence for a widespread, possible season ending frost/freeze for Saturday night into Sunday morning.
) Increasing confidence in strong high pressure building across the area promoting dry weather after Saturday and continuing for a long stretch of dry weather into next week.
